    "slot_value": "Require explicit, deliberate, and obvious operator confirmation before a critical command is executed; warning acknowledgment is specifically required when the action changes lane direction, affects a peak-period transition, or is being done under degraded conditions. It should pause for extra confirmation any time the action changes lane direction, starts a transition from a nonstandard state, proceeds under a warning condition, would override a currently active sequence, is being performed while the system is recovering from a communication outage, or while field devices are not fully synchronized yet. Special-event operations and any action outside the normal schedule should also require explicit acknowledgment that the operator is intentionally departing from standard operation, with a plain-language message explaining what is happening and what risk or dependency must be acknowledged before continuing.",
    "operation": "refine"
  },
  {
    "slot_number": "slot-3-1-2",
    "slot_key": "Preconditions before issuing a lane reversal command",
    "slot_value": "Operators need a clear, current picture of lane status, field devices, and whether anything is preventing the change before issuing a command; the system should also warn when the system or field devices are not in the right state and show enough context to explain why an action cannot proceed. They should only be able to open or close the lane when the system confirms the field devices are in a safe and expected state, when the relevant operational configuration for that period is active, and when there is no conflict, fault, or incomplete transition; otherwise the operator should be blocked or clearly warned before proceeding. The command should be rejected or delayed if the lane configuration does not match the allowed time window, if another control sequence is already in progress, if the system cannot confirm the devices are synchronized closely enough to proceed safely, or if there is a communications issue that makes status uncertain. The system should force a warning acknowledgment when the action changes lane direction, affects a peak-period transition, or is being done under degraded conditions, including when it would override an active sequence, when recovering from a communication outage, or when field devices are not fully synchronized. Special-event operations or any action outside the normal schedule should also be treated as requiring explicit acknowledgment of the deviation. For occasional operators, the screen should clearly show what action they are about to take, which lane direction or segment is affected, and what the current system and field-device status is before they proceed.",
    "operation": "refine"
  }
]

[
