    "slot_value": "A valid operator should still be blocked or warned if there is a conflicting active condition such as an interlock, device fault, incomplete prior transition, or an unsafe traffic-control state; in some cases the operator may proceed only after acknowledging the warning and confirming understanding of the risk, especially when the action changes the lane direction, starts a transition from a nonstandard state, or proceeds under a warning condition, and also when the command would override a currently active sequence, the system is recovering from a communication outage, the field devices are not fully synchronized yet, or the action is a special-event operation or otherwise outside the normal schedule; the system should pause for extra confirmation any time these conditions apply and should present a plain-language message explaining that the operator is intentionally departing from standard operation and needs to acknowledge it",
