    "slot_key": "Backup or fail-safe behavior during system degradation",
    "slot_value": "Safer coordination with other transportation systems and authorized users, with better operational visibility and reporting during degraded or difficult-to-obtain information conditions. Acceptance also requires that authorized users and approved partner systems can receive the right operational data under controlled access, and that the system works in normal and abnormal scenarios without workarounds. Full rollback is required if there is any doubt about command integrity, field-device synchronization, or operator visibility, especially during an active traffic period, with a clean return to the last known safe state before further changes. The system should delay commands when communications issues make status uncertain, and should force explicit warning acknowledgment before proceeding when changing lane direction, during peak-period transitions, or under degraded conditions. Extra confirmation is also required when a command would override an active sequence, when recovering from a communication outage, when field devices are not fully synchronized, and for special-event operations or any action outside the normal schedule.",
