    "slot_value": "Extra confirmation should be required when a lane command would override a currently active sequence, when the system is recovering from a communication outage, when field devices are not fully synchronized yet but the operator is trying to proceed anyway, and for special-event operations or any action outside the normal schedule.",
    "operation": "update"
  }
]

[
  {
    "slot_number": "slot-1-2-dyn-4",
    "slot_key": "Acceptance criteria for system replacement",
    "slot_value": "Operators can reliably perform core lane control functions, see accurate field and system status, generate required reports without losing essential operational capability, and authorized users and approved partner systems can receive the right operational data under controlled access. Acceptance also requires successful migration of agreed data, no critical defects in normal or exception operations, confirmation of security, logging, and recovery expectations, and the ability to run a normal operating period plus a special-event or abnormal scenario without workarounds. For peak-period or special-event operations, the new system must show the lane open and close sequence works end to end at the right times, with correct status feedback and no manual side steps; operators must be able to manage special-event setup, monitoring, and reporting exactly as needed; it must run with the same or better reliability than the legacy system; and the field devices and connected systems must stay in sync throughout. Extra confirmation is also needed when a command would override a currently active sequence, when the system is recovering from a communication outage, when field devices are not fully synchronized yet, and for special-event operations or any action outside the normal schedule.",
    "operation": "refine"
  }
]

[
