    "slot_key": "Communications uncertainty handling",
    "slot_value": "Any loss of communications to a critical element should be treated as safety-impacting if it prevents positive confirmation of lane status or prevents an essential control command from being sent. Uncertainty about a safety-critical state should be escalated immediately rather than left as a routine alarm. If confirmation is delayed, missing, or contradictory, operators should not treat the lane as safe to rely on automatically; the system should flag an alarm or uncertainty condition and require manual verification or fallback procedures before anyone acts on the result.",
