    "slot_key": "Immediate support and escalation contacts during cutover",
    "slot_value": "Operators should have a clearly identified primary support contact from the project or maintenance team, a District operations escalation contact who can make the immediate traffic decision if needed, and a path to the vendor or integrator for field-device issues. If the lane is still live and a quick traffic decision may be needed, it should escalate to District operations right away because they own the operational call. The primary support contact should stay engaged to diagnose and stabilize the system, but they should not make the traffic decision. The vendor or integrator should be brought in when the issue looks like a system defect, field-device fault, or anything requiring technical repair beyond what District staff can resolve. Minor operator-use issues can stay with the primary support contact if the lane state is stable. Any extension of added access after incident/cutover should also be confirmed by a supervisor or cutover lead before it stays in place.",
